                        </owl:intersectionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A mountain rising from the ocean seafloor that does not reach to the water&apos;s surface (sea level), and thus is not an island. Typically formed from volcanoes that rise abruptly and are usually found rising from a seafloor of 1,000 - 4,000 meters depth. Independent features that rise to at least 1,000 meters above the seafloor.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>mount</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EcoLexicon:mountain</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
