        <obo:IAO_0000115>Ocean acidification is a process during which the pH of a sea or ocean is lowered.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>LTER:962</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset>envoPolar</oboInOwl:inSubset>
        <rdfs:comment>On Earth, the major cause of ocean acidification is the update of carbon dioxide from the atmosphere.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ocean acidification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
