            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An estuarine coastal pycnocline which is composed primarily of fresh tidal water.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>What causes this freshwater layer to be &quot;tidal&quot; is not clearly specified in the current CMECS definition. Further, the original definition and label do not clearly state whether this is a pycnocline in its own right, or just the tidal freshwater part of the pycnocline. In this ENVO class, we follow the semantics suggested by the label and treat this as a type of estuarine coastal pycnocline.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CMECS:605</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://cmecscatalog.org/cmecs/classification/unit/605.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
