        <obo:IAO_0000115>An ice mass which forms a cohesive and contiguous sheet of water ice, floating upon the surface of a water body.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117 rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4366-3088"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>http://orcid.org/0000-0002-3410-4655</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>ice floes</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset>envoPolar</oboInOwl:inSubset>
        <rdfs:comment>Ice floes can exist in sea ice, in rivers or lakes. The WMO offers the following extent-based classification. Floe giant: Over 10 km across.
Floe vast: 2-10 km across. Floe big: 500-2000 m across. Floe medium: 100-500 m across. Floe small: 20-100 m across. Ice cake: Less than 20 m across. Small ice cake: Less than 2 m across.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ice floe</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_03000065"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An ice mass which forms a cohesive and contiguous sheet of water ice, floating upon the surface of a water body.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://nsidc.org/cryosphere/glossary/term/ice-floe</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_03000065"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Ice floes can exist in sea ice, in rivers or lakes. The WMO offers the following extent-based classification. Floe giant: Over 10 km across.
Floe vast: 2-10 km across. Floe big: 500-2000 m across. Floe medium: 100-500 m across. Floe small: 20-100 m across. Ice cake: Less than 20 m across. Small ice cake: Less than 2 m across.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>http://hdl.handle.net/11329/394</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


