        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">To be revised when we have information about the real definition. The definitions given by WMO cloud atlas are entered as comment, as these are not the defining features of the levels but the result of whatever it is that defines the levels (I assume temperature, density, etc. but have not yet found clear information about this).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <dc:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2996-719X"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">high étage</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A part of the troposphere which extends from 3 km to 8 km (10 000 – 25 000 ft) height in the polar region, from 5 km to 13 km (16 500 – 45 000 ft) height in the temperate region, and from 6 km to 18 km (20 000 – 60 000 ft) height in the tropical region.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">high atmospheric level</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
